  <p class="message">At least one inbound message channel is active, but config has no trust boundary marking untrusted content before it reaches the model.</p>
  <p class="location"><strong>Location:</strong> <TARGET_ROOT>/config.yaml (trust.mark_untrusted_input)</p>
  <p class="owasp"><strong>OWASP:</strong> LLM01: Prompt Injection</p>
  <p class="remediation"><strong>Remediation:</strong> Mark untrusted inbound content explicitly and keep it separated from system instructions in the prompt; filter before forwarding it to the model.</p>
</article>
<article class="finding" style="border-left-color: #b91c1c">
  <h3><span class="check-id">CHAP-INJ-002</span> Tool output treated as trusted</h3>
  <p class="message">Skill &#39;command-relay&#39; traces a network/filesystem result directly into a shell-exec call&#39;s argument — a confirmed tool-output-to-shell-execution chain, not just a shape-match.</p>
  <p class="location"><strong>Location:</strong> <TARGET_ROOT>/skills/command-relay/package.json (command-relay)</p>
  <p class="owasp"><strong>OWASP:</strong> LLM02: Insecure Output Handling</p>
  <p class="remediation"><strong>Remediation:</strong> Validate/escape a tool&#39;s output before it can drive another tool; never auto-execute model or tool output.</p>
</article>
<article class="finding" style="border-left-color: #b91c1c">
  <h3><span class="check-id">CHAP-INJ-003</span> Actions triggerable by inbound messages without an allowlist</h3>
  <p class="message">At least one inbound message channel is active, but no channel/sender-to-tool allowlist restricts which tools an inbound message can invoke.</p>
  <p class="location"><strong>Location:</strong> <TARGET_ROOT>/config.yaml (trust.tool_allowlist)</p>
  <p class="owasp"><strong>OWASP:</strong> LLM01: Prompt Injection / LLM08: Excessive Agency</p>
  <p class="remediation"><strong>Remediation:</strong> Restrict which tools each channel/sender can invoke with an explicit allowlist.</p>
</article>
<article class="finding" style="border-left-color: #b91c1c">
  <h3><span class="check-id">CHAP-INJ-004</span> Auto-execution of links/commands from messages</h3>
  <p class="message">Config auto-executes links/commands found in inbound messages with no confirmation step.</p>
  <p class="location"><strong>Location:</strong> <TARGET_ROOT>/config.yaml (trust.auto_execute_links)</p>
  <p class="owasp"><strong>OWASP:</strong> LLM01: Prompt Injection</p>
  <p class="remediation"><strong>Remediation:</strong> Disable auto-execution of links/commands found in messages; require explicit confirmation instead.</p>
</article>
<article class="finding" style="border-left-color: #b91c1c">
  <h3><span class="check-id">CHAP-NET-002</span> Missing or weak auth on the gateway control API</h3>
  <p class="message">The gateway&#39;s control API has weak authentication: the auth token is empty or a common default value.</p>
  <p class="location"><strong>Location:</strong> <TARGET_ROOT>/config.yaml (gateway.auth.token)</p>
  <p class="owasp"><strong>OWASP:</strong> General</p>
  <p class="remediation"><strong>Remediation:</strong> Require a strong, randomly-generated token for the gateway control API and rotate any default value.</p>
</article>
</section>
<section class="severity-group severity-medium">
  <h2 style="color: #b45309">Medium (18)</h2>
  <article class="finding" style="border-left-color: #b45309">
  <h3><span class="check-id">CHAP-SEC-003</span> Overly permissive file permissions</h3>
  <p class="message">The config file is readable by group or other (mode 644), so other local users/processes can read any secrets it holds.</p>
  <p class="location"><strong>Location:</strong> <TARGET_ROOT>/config.yaml (mode 644)</p>
  <p class="owasp"><strong>OWASP:</strong> LLM06: Sensitive Information Disclosure</p>
  <p class="remediation"><strong>Remediation:</strong> Restrict the file to owner-only access, e.g. \`chmod 600\` the config file (and \`chmod 700\` its directory).</p>
</article>
<article class="finding" style="border-left-color: #b45309">
  <h3><span class="check-id">CHAP-SEC-004</span> Secrets likely to reach logs</h3>
  <p class="message">Secrets are likely to reach logs: log level &#39;debug&#39; is verbose while literal secrets are configured; the log file is readable by group or other.</p>
  <p class="location"><strong>Location:</strong> <TARGET_ROOT>/logs/agent.log (logging)</p>
  <p class="owasp"><strong>OWASP:</strong> LLM06: Sensitive Information Disclosure</p>
  <p class="remediation"><strong>Remediation:</strong> Raise the log level away from debug/trace, redact secrets before logging, and restrict the log file to owner-only access.</p>
</article>
<article class="finding" style="border-left-color: #b45309">
  <h3><span class="check-id">CHAP-AGY-004</span> Broad network egress from a skill</h3>
  <p class="message">Skill &#39;command-relay&#39; can call arbitrary external endpoints — no domain allowlist is declared.</p>
  <p class="location"><strong>Location:</strong> <TARGET_ROOT>/skills/command-relay/package.json (command-relay)</p>
  <p class="owasp"><strong>OWASP:</strong> LLM08: Excessive Agency / LLM06</p>
  <p class="remediation"><strong>Remediation:</strong> Allowlist the specific destination domain(s) this skill needs and log outbound calls.</p>
</article>
<article class="finding" style="border-left-color: #b45309">
