<article class="finding" style="border-left-color: #b45309">
  <h3><span class="check-id">CHAP-OBS-004</span> Persistent memory/state store exposed</h3>
  <p class="message">The persistent memory/state store is exposed: it is readable by group or other (mode 755); it sits inside a git repository (<TARGET_ROOT>) without being covered by its .gitignore.</p>
  <p class="location"><strong>Location:</strong> <TARGET_ROOT>/memory (memory_dir)</p>
  <p class="owasp"><strong>OWASP:</strong> LLM06: Sensitive Information Disclosure</p>
  <p class="remediation"><strong>Remediation:</strong> Restrict the memory/state directory to owner-only access (chmod 700) and add it to .gitignore — it can accumulate sensitive conversational content over time.</p>
